{
  "id": "library/expenses",
  "category": "finance",
  "replaces": "Expense tracker and budget planner",
  "title": "Expenses",
  "summary": "Spending, income, accounts, budgets and subscriptions, offline and ad-free.",
  "description": "**Expenses** keeps your spending, income, accounts and budgets on your phone, without an account, ads or a subscription.\n\n### Everyday\n- **Add an entry in a few taps:** the amount on a calculator keypad (12,40 + 3,10 works), a category, the account and the date are already picked, so most entries are the amount and Save. Quick-add buttons for the categories you use most, \"Add again today\", notes, payees and tags with suggestions.\n- **Spending, income and transfers** between your accounts: cash, bank accounts, cards and savings, each with its balance, a running balance per account, and the total of everything.\n- **Safe to spend today:** what is left of this month's budget shared out over the days left, minus what you spent today. On the home screen and on a home-screen widget; it updates at midnight.\n- **Budgets** for the whole month and for any category (subcategories count toward their category), with a warning when one is nearly used up or over.\n- **Categories with icons and colours, and subcategories.** Hide what you no longer use; deleting one moves its entries first.\n- **Recurring entries** such as rent, salary and bills: added for you on their date, or a notification with Add and Skip, or only tracked.\n- **Subscription finder:** spots payments that repeat with the same amount (in imported history too) and shows what they cost a month and a year. Confirm, edit or dismiss each one.\n\n### See where it goes\n- The month at a glance, month by month and year by year, a ring chart by category, spending day by day, the last 12 months of spending and income, and a calendar with each day's total.\n- Search notes, payees, categories, tags and amounts; filter by period, type, category, account, tag and amount; export what you found.\n\n### Your data\n- **Bring your history:** imports the CSV file most money and budget apps export, and spreadsheets: comma, semicolon or tab; day-first or month-first dates; decimal commas or points. Spending, income and transfers are all kept (a type, income or transfer column, separate income amounts, signed amounts, or the two halves of a transfer); missing categories, subcategories and accounts are created; you see which rows could not be read, and one tap undoes the import.\n- **Several currencies** with rates you type yourself: each entry keeps its own amount and rate, and totals are shown in your main currency. Nothing is fetched from the internet.\n- Export everything, a period or a search to CSV. Receipt photos from the camera or your pictures. Everything is in Zapli's backup of your apps.\n- **In English and Slovak**, euro first, with each language's number and date formats.\n\n### What it never does\n- No ads, no tracking, no analytics, no account, no sign-in, no upsells.\n- It cannot connect to the internet, and there is no bank connection: nothing leaves your phone unless you export a file.\n\n### Privacy\nAmounts are marked as financial data, so notifications and the widget hide them on a locked screen. An optional app lock keeps everything behind your fingerprint, face or screen lock; turn it on in the app's permissions.",
  "license": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
